Let's tackle the second issue: **The Master Data "DB Hammer"** in **ValidationMasterService.java**.
When 10 users upload files at once, your VoucherBulkValidationService runs runDbCheck, which asks this master service for all the Branches, Currencies, and CGLs. Without caching, your backend will blast the Oracle database with 30 heavy SELECT queries at the exact same millisecond.
Since you already set up a beautiful Redis @EnableCaching architecture in your CacheConfig.java, we just need to activate it here!
### The Fix
Open **ValidationMasterService.java**. You just need to add the @Cacheable annotation to your three methods.
Here is the updated class. Replace your existing methods with these:
```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Service;

import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Qualifier;
import org.springframework.cache.annotation.Cacheable;
import org.springframework.dao.DataAccessException;
import org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Set;

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class ValidationMasterService {

    @Autowired
    @Qualifier("oracleJdbcTemplate")
    private JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;

    /**
     * Fetches all active branch codes.
     * Cached in Redis to prevent database hammering during concurrent bulk uploads.
     */
    @Cacheable(value = "master_branches", unless = "#result.isEmpty()")
    public Set<String> getAllActiveBranches() {
        long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
        String sql = "SELECT CODE FROM BRANCH_MASTER WHERE STATUS = 1";

        try {
            List<String> list = jdbcTemplate.query(con -> {
                var ps = con.prepareStatement(sql);
                ps.setFetchSize(5000);
                return ps;
            }, (rs, rowNum) -> rs.getString(1));

            log.info("MASTER_DATA_LOADED | Type: BRANCHES | Count: {} | Duration: {}ms", list.size(), System.currentTimeMillis() - start);
            return new HashSet<>(list);

        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("MASTER_DATA_FETCH_FAIL | Type: BRANCHES | Reason: {}", e.getMessage());
            return new HashSet<>(); 
        }
    }

    /**
     * Fetches all active currency codes.
     */
    @Cacheable(value = "master_currencies", unless = "#result.isEmpty()")
    public Set<String> getAllActiveCurrencies() {
        long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
        String sql = "SELECT CURRENCY_CODE FROM CURRENCY_MASTER WHERE FLAG = 1";

        try {
            List<String> list = jdbcTemplate.query(con -> {
                var ps = con.prepareStatement(sql);
                ps.setFetchSize(1000);
                return ps;
            }, (rs, rowNum) -> rs.getString(1));

            log.info("MASTER_DATA_LOADED | Type: CURRENCIES | Count: {} | Duration: {}ms", list.size(), System.currentTimeMillis() - start);
            return new HashSet<>(list);

        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("MASTER_DATA_FETCH_FAIL | Type: CURRENCIES | Reason: {}", e.getMessage());
            return new HashSet<>();
        }
    }

    /**
     * Fetches all active CGL numbers.
     */
    @Cacheable(value = "master_cgls", unless = "#result.isEmpty()")
    public Set<String> getAllActiveCgls() {
        long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
        String sql = "SELECT CGL_NUMBER FROM CGL_MASTER WHERE STATUS = 1";

        try {
            List<String> list = jdbcTemplate.query(con -> {
                var ps = con.prepareStatement(sql);
                ps.setFetchSize(2000);
                return ps;
            }, (rs, rowNum) -> rs.getString(1));

            log.info("MASTER_DATA_LOADED | Type: CGLS | Count: {} | Duration: {}ms", list.size(), System.currentTimeMillis() - start);
            return new HashSet<>(list);

        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("MASTER_DATA_FETCH_FAIL | Type: CGLS | Reason: {}", e.getMessage());
            return new HashSet<>();
        }
    }
}

```
### Why this is the perfect implementation:
Notice the unless = "#result.isEmpty()" parameter. This is a crucial safety net! If the Oracle database blips for a split second and returns an empty list, this prevents Spring from caching that empty list into Redis (which would cause all subsequent uploads to fail validation). It ensures only valid, populated master data is kept in memory.
